cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this data or code, please cite the paper below."
title: "A property-registry contract for retrieve-or-refuse thermal-mechanical lattice search"
abstract: >-
  An engineer's sentence is compiled against a declared property registry into a
  typed query over a catalogue of solved metal-cell combinations. A non-empty
  feasible set returns a catalogue row that a second solver can rebuild; an empty
  one returns minimal unsatisfiable subsets and the slack of a repair rather than
  the nearest row.
